{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: added explicit `sigma_a ~ uniform(0, 100)` and `sigma_y ~ uniform(0, 100)` statements so the finite bounded scale parameters have exactly one built-in SafeStan prior before use. These make the original implicit proper uniform priors from `real<lower=0, upper=100>` explicit. No data fields were added or changed; `J`, `N`, `county`, and `u` are unprotected context inputs.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> J;
  int<lower=0> N;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=J> county;
  vector[N] u;
  vector[N] y;
}
parameters {
  vector[J] a;
  real b;
  real mu_a;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_a;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_y;
}
transformed parameters {
  vector[N] y_hat;

  for (i in 1 : N) {
    y_hat[i] = a[county[i]] + u[i] * b * 0.1;
  }
}
model {
  mu_a ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma_a ~ uniform(0, 100);
  a ~ normal(mu_a, sigma_a);
  b ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma_y ~ uniform(0, 100);
  y ~ normal(y_hat, sigma_y);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"J":1,"N":2,"county":[1,1],"u":[5.3406067274867635,4.728868607808346],"y":[2.0,2.0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
